   "*9.13 before *9.21 or *9.22"
  ],
  "reason": "For elementary p and every function phi it is distribEl (PM/Found9/Base.lean). For a p with apparent variables the two sides can be the same proposition (p = (Eu).chi u, phi elementary: both are (x):(Eu).chi u v phi x, pinned in Checks/PinnedStatements.lean) or differ (p = (Eu).chi u, phi x = (w).psi(x,w): distrib_sides_ne). Rep.distrib (PM/Found9/FromStar10.lean) proves it for every p given Rep and a variable of every type; an instance whose two sides are the same proposition needs neither.",
  "glue": [],
  "glue_kind": []
 },
